## What I inspected and played
- Headless Chromium (Playwright 1.64), served by `python3 -m http.server`, real-time arrow-key play (script in my working dir, results in `acceptance/notes.md`, captures in `acceptance/build3/`), repeated on the final assembly: title on load (arrows do not start, Enter does); 5 foods each +1 length / +1 score with live HUD; quick double turn applied, reversal ignored; wall death with final score matching; Play again resets to score 0 / length 3 without reload; page never scrolls; zero console messages, all assets loaded.
- Viewports 800x500, 1024x600, 1366x650, 1280x720, 1920x1080: HUD and full board inside the window, no scroll.
- Read `src/logic.js`: grid rules, food on free cells only, wall and self collision (tail cell vacated when not eating), 180° reversal guard, 2-turn buffer.

